    2. Pick 3 colors (frame, fill, sprite_color); sprite_color may equal frame
    3. Design a small sprite (1-2 rows x 2-3 cols, 2-5 pixels of sprite_color, rest fill)
    4. Choose delta in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} and a starting top_row such that ALL panel positions
       AND the extrapolated output position fit within rows [1, h-2]
       Extrapolated top = last_top + delta * panel_w / (panel_w - 1), rounded half-up
    5. Build output panel: frame border, fill interior, sprite at extrapolated row
    6. Build input: concatenate num_panels panels sharing border columns, each with sprite
       at top_row + i*delta (i=0..n-1), same local column
